{%- comment -%}
  The homepage body (home-body.liquid) for the locale home pages, which are Markdown pages: Markdown pages are in the
  collections, whose urls tell the localize step that a locale translates the root page (an HTML page would get
  the root index.html copied over it as a fallback). The body is written as one raw region (Douze's markdown: a line
  that starts and ends with U+001E is HTML written as it is, its U+001D characters being newlines), so that the
  Markdown pass keeps it as it is: it would otherwise end the HTML blocks at the blank lines of the code samples.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture hpr_newline %}
{% endcapture -%}
{%- capture hpr_body %}{% include "partials/home/home-body.liquid" %}{% endcapture -%}
{{ hpr_body | strip | replace: hpr_newline, "" | raw }}
